DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ggeettpptt() opens a new pseudoterminal device and returns a file descriptor
       that refers to that device.  It is equivalent to opening the pseudoter‐
       minal multiplexor device

           open("/dev/ptmx", O_RDWR);

       on  Linux  systems, though the pseudoterminal multiplexor device is lo‐
       cated elsewhere on some systems that use the GNU C library.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       ggeettpptt() returns an open file  descriptor  upon  successful  completion.
       Otherwise, it returns -1 and sets _e_r_r_n_o to indicate the error.

